{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into sensing and motion capability so the supervisor can react to uncontrollable obstacle observations before issuing one-shot motion pulses. The specifications enforce a deterministic exploration policy: random_walk in clear/search, short move_forward only in a dedicated progress state, obstacle-front to dedicated turn recovery, side-obstacle to consistent directed turns, and rapid return to exploration once path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear to respect pre-action uncontrollable processing, while obstacle events preempt to safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capabilities in G, then encode policy in small deterministic E automata",
    "Use one-shot commit states with exactly one controllable action each, favor random_walk in clear exploration, and force obstacle-triggered turn recovery before any return to exploration"
